                    <Paragraph>If you work through it, I think you’ll find out that you end up getting a lot of little implied types that have to exist, but would exist unnamed. And I think this type system sort of bottoms out at canonicals, where if you end up with a type with nothing that inherits from it, it is an instance, it is the canonical of itself, and possibly the canonical of the type above it, and with a finite number of things, you can probably always bottom out on those. But I bet you need a ton of them! All of them are implied. They could be added but philosophically SRT says that you didn’t referred to it yet so you better add a word or phrase for it before you can</Paragraph>
